From: fyde-nix
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: keep the Hantro VPU disabled on FydeTab Duo

rk3588s-mpp.dtsi disables the upstream Hantro node because the vendor MPP
stack drives the same register window (vepu@fdb50000, a separate node with
a different compatible). The board file re-enabled it, so hantro-vpu tried
to request IRQ 119 while IRQ 120 was already in use, failing with "Could
not request default IRQ" and leaving two drivers bound to one block.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-fydetab_duo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-fydetab_duo.dts
@@ -664,8 +664,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The vendor MPP stack drives vepu@fdb50000 (the other node in this register
+ * window), so keep the upstream Hantro node disabled as rk3588s-mpp.dtsi
+ * intends. Enabling it makes hantro-vpu fail to request its IRQ and leaves
+ * two drivers fighting over the same block.
+ */
 &vpu121 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &vpu121_mmu {
